# CrimsonC9 — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Never commit .env.local — it's already in .gitignore, and it's the actual thing
# this file exists to keep out of git.
#
# This is the LOCAL DEV list. Production runs in Docker on the Hetzner server and reads
# its own file, `/opt/c9-website/deploy/prod/.env` — template in `deploy/prod/.env.example`.
# The two are not the same list: production needs ZEPTOMAIL_TOKEN and IMAGE_TAG, local dev
# needs neither.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required — nothing. The site runs with an empty .env.local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# DATABASE_URI and PAYLOAD_SECRET used to be required here. The landing page was decoupled
# from Payload for v1, so no route reads them any more — they are only needed if you bring
# `src/app/_payload` back into routing to work on the CMS. `src/payload.config.ts` still
# throws without them, which is how you'll find out.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — the app has a working fallback if these are unset
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The canonical public URL of the deployed site — used for CORS, email links, and
# media URLs. Leave unset in local dev; payload.config.ts falls back to
# http://localhost:3000 automatically. Vercel sets this in the dashboard for
# Preview/Production (falls back further to its own auto-generated VERCEL_URL if
# that's ever missed).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=

# ZeptoMail (Zoho) API token — sends the notification email when somebody submits the
# landing page's collaboration form (src/lib/zeptomail.ts). Same provider as the ticket
# shop, which is why there is no second set of DKIM/SPF records on crimsonc9.com.
#
# Unset is a supported state locally: the endpoint answers 502 and writes the full enquiry
# to the server log, so nothing is lost and the visitor is told to use the address under
# the form. In production that log is the only copy — there is no database row behind it
# any more — so this is effectively required on the server.
#
# Paste it with or without the "Zoho-enczapikey " prefix the Zoho UI shows; both work.
# ZEPTOMAIL_TOKEN=

# Sender address. Must be on a domain verified in the ZeptoMail account, or every send
# fails with a 4xx that reads like a code bug. Defaults to
# "CrimsonC9 <noreply@crimsonc9.com>".
# EMAIL_FROM=

# Override the API endpoint. Defaults to the EU data centre
# (https://api.zeptomail.eu/v1.1/email) — the documented default is a different host, and
# a token issued in the EU account does not work against it.
# ZEPTOMAIL_API_URL=

# Where form notifications are delivered. Defaults to hello@crimsonc9.com. Worth
# overriding anywhere test submissions are made, so they don't land in the real inbox.
# C9_NOTIFY_EMAIL=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Coming soon — not wired into the code yet, listed so the shape is known ahead
# of time. Don't set these until the corresponding feature actually lands; an
# unused env var sitting around with a stale value is its own small trap.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backblaze B2 media storage (ADR-0004, docs/concepts/CONCEPT_media-pipeline.md).
# Needed once @payloadcms/storage-s3 is actually installed and configured — right
# now Payload still writes uploads to the local filesystem, which doesn't survive
# a Vercel redeploy. Bucket-scoped application key, not the account master key.
# S3_ENDPOINT=
# S3_REGION=
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Ticketing — nothing goes here. The shop is a separate app on its own subdomain
# (C9DevOne/c9-tickets → tickets.crimsonc9.com) with its own environment; this site only
# ever links to it. ADR-0009 still says "Pretix, infrastructure undecided" and needs
# superseding.
